    <string name="focus_outside">outside the launcher</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_explain">Timers and focus mode stop apps opened from OmaLauncher++. To stop them wherever they\'re opened, from a notification, another app or Recents, turn on OmaLauncher++ focus in Android\'s accessibility settings. It reads only which app comes to the front, never what\'s on screen or what you type, and Settings, the phone app and the keyboard are never stopped. Android may ask you first to allow restricted settings in the launcher\'s app info, as it does for apps not from a store. It\'s off unless you turn it on.</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_on">on</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_off">off</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_open">accessibility settings</string>
    <string name="focus_file_hint">Agents can edit all of this in ~/.config/omalauncher/focus/focus.toml.</string>

    <string name="focus_guard_label">OmaLauncher++ focus</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_summary">Focus mode and app timers for apps opened outside the launcher</string>
    <string name="focus_guard_description">Lets OmaLauncher++\'s focus mode and app timers stop apps opened outside the launcher: from a notification, another app or Recents. It reads only which app comes to the front, never what\'s on screen or what you type, and nothing leaves the phone. Settings, the phone app and the keyboard are never stopped.</string>

